  "india_reference_works": 2255438,
  "findings": [
    "Among our labs, CSIR-CCMB has the highest mean FWCI (2.05, 95% CI 1.57-2.63), ranking 4 of 17 institutes; the peer median is 1.98.",
    "1 of our 4 labs has a mean FWCI above the peer median; the top mean belongs to NIBMG (3.77, citation Gini 0.90, i.e. driven by a few very highly cited papers), while on the outlier-robust median FWCI the leader is NIPGR (1.31) and our labs rank CSIR-CDRI 7, CSIR-IGIB 13, CSIR-CCMB 14, CSIR-IMTECH 16 of 17.",
    "Our labs' share of papers in the global top 10% by citations ranges from 13.3% (CSIR-CDRI) to 14.3% (CSIR-IGIB), against a peer median of 17.8%.",
    "CSIR-CDRI has the largest output of all 17 institutes (3,386 articles and reviews, 314 a year, 2.5 times the median peer), yet ranks 14 of 17 on mean FWCI.",
    "Output growth from the first year to the last complete year runs from -3.5% a year (CSIR-IMTECH) to -1.1% a year (CSIR-CCMB) in our labs, against a peer median of 0.8%; a log-linear trend over all complete years gives -2.2% to 0.2% for our labs vs 2.7% for the median peer.",
    "International co-authorship is 16.4%-28.9% of papers in our labs and 27.9% at the median peer; open access is 32.5%-66.4% vs 60.4%.",
    "Citations are concentrated everywhere (Gini 0.61-0.90); in CSIR-CCMB (Gini 0.76) a few papers carry the totals, the citation weight of only 49 'effective' papers out of 1,698.",
    "Relative to all Indian output, the strongest specialisations are CSIR-CCMB in Genetics (RCA 15.5); CSIR-IGIB in Immunology and Allergy (RCA 39.4); CSIR-IMTECH in Structural Biology (RCA 57.7); CSIR-CDRI in Organic Chemistry (RCA 10.9).",
    "Within India, joint papers fall with distance with elasticity -0.58 (95% CI -0.64 to -0.51) and citations with -0.30 (-0.35 to -0.26): collaboration decays with distance more steeply than citation (difference -0.27, p = 3.4e-44)."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "FWCI and citation percentiles are OpenAlex's own field-and-year normalisations; they are missing for a few papers (FWCI coverage 99.8%-100.0% across institutes), are recomputed by OpenAlex over time, and recent years have had little time to accumulate citations.",
    "Lineage counts include students, postdocs, project staff and every affiliate rolled up to the institute, and child institutions in the OpenAlex hierarchy; output is not comparable with our faculty-only corpus.",
    "Peers differ in size, mission (basic vs translational vs plant or toxicology) and field mix; FWCI and percentiles normalise by field, raw citations and h-index do not, and h-index grows with output.",
    "RCA is measured against ALL Indian output, which is dominated by engineering, physical and computer sciences, so most life-science subfields have RCA far above 1 and small niche subfields (a few dozen papers) can top the list; compare institutes within a subfield rather than reading the absolute level.",
    "2026 is a partial year: it is counted in totals but excluded from CAGR, papers per year and RCA.",
    "Gravity model: partner institutions are those already linked to our faculty corpus by co-authorship or citation (zeros only arise across labs), coordinates are OpenAlex's city-level geocodes, and partner size is OpenAlex's all-time works count; standard errors are robust (sandwich) because counts are overdispersed.",
    "OpenAlex affiliation parsing is imperfect: missing or wrong institution links move papers between institutes."
  ],
  "methods": {
    "works_query": "authorships.institutions.lineage:<id>, publication_year window, type article|review, is_retracted:false; identical for all institutes",
    "papers_per_year": "mean over 2016-2025",
    "trend_growth": "exp(slope) - 1 of log(papers) on year, 2016-2025",
    "cagr": "(papers 2025 / papers 2016)^(1/9) - 1",
    "fwci": "mean and median over papers with FWCI; mean CI = percentile bootstrap, 1000 resamples, seed 42",
    "top_shares": "citation_normalized_percentile.is_in_top_10_percent / is_in_top_1_percent over papers with a percentile; Wilson 95% CI",
    "intl_share": "countries_distinct_count > 1; Wilson CI",
    "oa_share": "open_access.is_oa; Wilson CI",
    "concentration": "Gini of paper citations; effective papers = (sum c)^2 / sum c^2",
    "diversity": "distinct primary-topic subfields; Shannon entropy (natural log) of subfield shares",
    "ranks": "1 = highest among all institutes (ours + peers), ties share the lower rank",
    "rca": "(institute share of subfield) / (India share), 2016-2025, primary topic subfield; India = institutions.country_code:IN with the same type and retraction filters (group_by paged by cursor); subfields with >= 15 institute papers",
    "gravity": "Poisson GLM by IRLS: count ~ log(distance_km + 10) + log(partner works_count) + lab fixed effects, over every (lab, partner) pair for Indian partner institutions (not our labs or their children, not umbrella or academy rows) that co-author with or cite any lab; joint papers = faculty-corpus papers of the lab with an author at the partner; citations = (citing paper, cited lab paper) links from inflow works with an author at the partner; robust sandwich SEs; difference test uses the cross-score covariance of the two fits"
  },
  "openalex": "OpenAlex calls: 0 live, 186 cached"
}